  "id": "inhibition",
  "term": "inhibition",
  "definition": "In this source, inhibition refers to response inhibition: the ability to suppress or stop a motor action when circumstances change. It can happen before a movement starts or by interrupting a movement already in progress, helping behavior stay safe and adaptive.",
